WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/vehicles/pages/VehicleDetailPage.tsx, route /vehicles/:id. The vehicle-detail page:
    Queries        : useVehicleSettings(vehicleId) → GET /vehicles/{id}/settings (the manifest's declared data
                     source) feeds the title via findEffectiveSetting(settings,'nickname'); effectiveName =
                     (nickname.value string & non-empty) ?? vehicle.display_name ?? t('vehicles.detail.title').
                     (The page also issues many sibling live queries — state/motor/climate/security/tire/charging-
                     telemetry/drives/charging/vehicle-config — whose sub-components are SEPARATE parity units;
                     the page unit's declared sources are useVehicleSettings + findEffectiveSetting.)
    Wake           : wakeMutation → POST /vehicles/{id}/wake; onSuccess toast t('vehicles.detail.wakeSuccess'),
                     onError toast t('vehicles.detail.wakeFailed').
    Loading        : vehicleLoading → <VehicleDetailSkeleton/> (page header + panel + 2 stat grids + chart + tables).
    Error          : vehicleError → PageContainer error.
    Body           : <LiveStaleDataBanner/> + LiveIndicator(compact) + a header in a SectionErrorBoundary
                     (fallbackTitle headerFailed); then `!state` → <GlassPanel className="p-8"><Skeleton/></GlassPanel>
                     (this is GlassPanel1), else fifteen SectionErrorBoundary-wrapped sections, each with its own
                     fallbackTitle: batteryRange, liveState, quickStats, motor, climate, security, tire,
                     chargingTelemetry, batteryCharts, recentDrives, recentCharges, vehicleConfig, aiPaintPreview,
                     quickLinks, settings.

